  "worked_solution": "First, we need to find the volume of one storage unit.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=9,\\,w=24,\\,h=8\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=9\\cdot 24\\cdot 8=1\\,728\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total volume of the ten storage units is\n\n$$\n1\\,728\\cdot 10=17\\,280\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}.\n$$",
